shionable for men and women; Coco Chanel helped popularize it among women, and wearers included Harold Lloyd and Maurice Chevalier.[1] \"Straw Hat Day\" marked the start of summer, culminating in the 1922 Straw Hat Riot in New York.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1922","event":"Straw Hat Riot in New York City.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Boater","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boater","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Affirmative Action","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/affirmative-action/43268","site":"T Nation · 147 posts · 2005"},{"title":"Bushworld","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/bushworld/40486","site":"T Nation · 122 posts · 2004"},{"title":"Bad Comedy Movies","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/bad-comedy-movies/165099","site":"T Nation · 82 posts · 2011"}]}